1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,900
What happens when three million people lose

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:03,000
their life savings overnight?

3
00:00:03,399 --> 00:00:06,099
Meet Ueno, a homegrown digital bank that

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,299
became deeply embedded in Paraguay's payments

5
00:00:08,199 --> 00:00:08,679
system.

6
00:00:08,926 --> 00:00:11,186
So this app just won over half the country?

7
00:00:11,427 --> 00:00:14,467
Exactly! It offered a sleek interface for

8
00:00:14,367 --> 00:00:16,487
those underserved by brick-and-mortar banks.

9
00:00:16,771 --> 00:00:17,591
Until it didn't?

10
00:00:17,686 --> 00:00:19,905
Until regulators stepped in. The solvency

11
00:00:19,805 --> 00:00:21,925
ratio fell below half the legal minimum.

12
00:00:22,276 --> 00:00:25,256
Reuters reported around $850 million in

13
00:00:25,156 --> 00:00:26,976
public funds administered by the lender.

14
00:00:27,370 --> 00:00:29,510
We just shifted to a resolution process

15
00:00:29,410 --> 00:00:30,630
on November 3rd.

16
00:00:30,719 --> 00:00:32,699
Which means your mobile app, cards, and

17
00:00:32,599 --> 00:00:34,939
transfers are completely frozen right now.

18
00:00:34,996 --> 00:00:37,096
But the Central Bank inspectors found poorly

19
00:00:36,996 --> 00:00:38,956
documented loans to connected companies!

20
00:00:39,370 --> 00:00:41,430
Wait, can people just get their money back?

21
00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:44,950
Deposit insurance covers up to roughly $35,000

22
00:00:44,850 --> 00:00:45,589
per customer.

23
00:00:45,807 --> 00:00:46,947
Does that mean everyone is safe?

24
00:00:47,188 --> 00:00:49,747
It covers the full balances of an estimated

25
00:00:49,647 --> 00:00:52,668
97 percent. The rest are waiting.

26
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,840
When branches closed and apps stopped working,

27
00:00:56,179 --> 00:00:58,160
a rush to open accounts elsewhere disrupted

28
00:00:58,060 --> 00:00:59,259
other banks' systems.

29
00:00:59,653 --> 00:01:02,573
Demonstrators marched through Asunción demanding

30
00:01:02,473 --> 00:01:04,693
their savings and accountability from the

31
00:01:04,593 --> 00:01:04,953
government.

32
00:01:05,346 --> 00:01:08,286
The lower house voted 78 in favor of impeachment

33
00:01:08,186 --> 00:01:09,406
on November 5th.

34
00:01:09,381 --> 00:01:11,522
But President Peña submitted his resignation

35
00:01:11,422 --> 00:01:14,002
a day earlier! Why push forward?

36
00:01:14,269 --> 00:01:16,509
Because the Senate proceeded with the trial.

37
00:01:16,829 --> 00:01:18,689
The vote was 44 to zero.

38
00:01:19,074 --> 00:01:21,493
A unanimous removal? That's a political

39
00:01:21,393 --> 00:01:21,974
landslide!

40
00:01:22,479 --> 00:01:24,899
Lawmakers accused Peña's government of allowing

41
00:01:24,799 --> 00:01:28,179
$355 million from the state pension fund

42
00:01:28,079 --> 00:01:30,219
to be deposited beyond legal limits.

43
00:01:30,579 --> 00:01:32,679
So does the resignation save his legal standing?

44
00:01:32,915 --> 00:01:35,974
Under Article 189, resignation would grant

45
00:01:35,875 --> 00:01:37,955
a lifetime Senate seat and immunity.

46
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:39,849
And because they impeached him instead?

47
00:01:40,109 --> 00:01:42,648
Precisely. He was stripped of protections

48
00:01:42,548 --> 00:01:44,869
and placed under house arrest on November

49
00:01:44,769 --> 00:01:45,508
6th.

50
00:01:45,706 --> 00:01:47,846
Prosecutors charged him with breach of trust

51
00:01:47,746 --> 00:01:49,846
and administration for personal gain the

52
00:01:49,746 --> 00:01:50,566
very next day.

53
00:01:50,823 --> 00:01:52,983
Peña's attorney argued that ousting a president

54
00:01:52,883 --> 00:01:55,443
during a bank resolution could destabilize

55
00:01:55,343 --> 00:01:56,343
the financial system.

56
00:01:56,616 --> 00:01:58,156
Did his own party abandon him?

57
00:01:58,362 --> 00:02:00,962
Former president Horacio Cartes withdrew

58
00:02:00,862 --> 00:02:03,822
support, calling it the plundering of pensioners'

59
00:02:03,802 --> 00:02:04,062
money.

60
00:02:04,348 --> 00:02:05,408
So he's completely alone?

61
00:02:05,674 --> 00:02:07,813
He sent lawyers to the Senate but refused

62
00:02:07,713 --> 00:02:10,414
to attend himself. A political isolation.

63
00:02:10,866 --> 00:02:13,286
What about Carlos Carvallo? He led the central

64
00:02:13,186 --> 00:02:14,106
bank after all.

65
00:02:14,199 --> 00:02:16,619
He was also charged with breach of trust

66
00:02:16,519 --> 00:02:19,519
and producing false documents. Pretrial

67
00:02:19,419 --> 00:02:20,559
detention approved.

68
00:02:20,813 --> 00:02:22,932
So both the president and the regulator

69
00:02:22,832 --> 00:02:23,553
are down?

70
00:02:23,781 --> 00:02:26,300
Investigators are examining whether officials

71
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:28,201
failed to act on warning signs.

72
00:02:28,566 --> 00:02:30,786
A judge ordered Peña held at a military

73
00:02:30,686 --> 00:02:33,106
facility, marking the second Paraguayan

74
00:02:33,006 --> 00:02:35,026
president removed via impeachment since

75
00:02:34,926 --> 00:02:35,666
1989.

76
00:02:36,259 --> 00:02:37,099
Who takes over now?

77
00:02:37,277 --> 00:02:39,877
Vice-President Pedro Alliana was sworn in

78
00:02:39,777 --> 00:02:42,837
to complete the term until August 2028.

79
00:02:43,083 --> 00:02:44,143
Is he safe from scrutiny?

80
00:02:44,450 --> 00:02:46,870
He is also under investigation in connection

81
00:02:46,770 --> 00:02:49,590
with the bank. Political uncertainty remains.

82
00:02:50,093 --> 00:02:52,073
The Central Bank estimates the guarantee

83
00:02:51,973 --> 00:02:54,873
covers around 97 percent of Ueno's customers.

84
00:02:55,259 --> 00:02:57,439
Authorities have promised that depositors

85
00:02:57,339 --> 00:02:58,879
will be reimbursed entirely.

86
00:02:59,308 --> 00:03:00,908
How much has been returned so far?

87
00:03:01,124 --> 00:03:04,744
The equivalent of $160 million paid out

88
00:03:04,644 --> 00:03:07,044
to nearly 1.2 million savers.

89
00:03:07,363 --> 00:03:09,923
That's progress, but analysts warn the damage

90
00:03:09,823 --> 00:03:11,242
to reputation may linger.

91
00:03:11,619 --> 00:03:13,979
This is the moment when Paraguay must demonstrate

92
00:03:13,879 --> 00:03:15,719
that its institutions are functioning.

93
00:03:16,069 --> 00:03:19,009
Peña denied wrongdoing, while a state electricity

94
00:03:18,909 --> 00:03:21,469
worker called the crisis an enormous betrayal

95
00:03:21,370 --> 00:03:21,989
of trust.

96
00:03:22,330 --> 00:03:24,110
How do people even describe this mess?

97
00:03:24,457 --> 00:03:26,695
An economist called it a modern-day Bonnie

98
00:03:26,596 --> 00:03:29,736
and Clyde. They didn't rob us with a pistol.

99
00:03:30,110 --> 00:03:31,730
They robbed us with an app? Seriously?

100
00:03:32,144 --> 00:03:35,584
Exactly. A sleek app, a hidden shortfall,

101
00:03:35,844 --> 00:03:37,584
and a political domino effect.

102
00:03:37,990 --> 00:03:39,969
So no more lifetime senate seats for failed

103
00:03:39,870 --> 00:03:40,250
presidents?

104
00:03:40,694 --> 00:03:43,854
Impeachment strips that protection. Democracy

105
00:03:43,754 --> 00:03:45,394
isn't a revolving door.

106
00:03:45,638 --> 00:03:47,198
I guess keeping your accounts safe matters

107
00:03:47,098 --> 00:03:48,217
more than political perks?

108
00:03:48,539 --> 00:03:51,259
Without public funds, the whole system collapses.

109
00:03:51,737 --> 00:03:52,639
It really does.

110
00:03:53,056 --> 00:03:55,196
Next time I'll just stick to physical branches

111
00:03:55,096 --> 00:03:56,296
and paper receipts.

112
00:03:56,607 --> 00:03:59,807
Better yet, check your solvency ratios before

113
00:03:59,707 --> 00:04:00,447
you go viral.

114
00:04:00,744 --> 00:04:02,944
Don't worry, my app is perfectly regulated.

115
00:04:03,224 --> 00:04:04,784
I swear on my coffee machine!

116
00:04:05,183 --> 00:04:06,843
That's the story of how a banking glitch

117
00:04:06,743 --> 00:04:08,723
toppled a government. Thanks for watching!

118
00:04:08,864 --> 00:04:10,784
Like and subscribe before I check my own

119
00:04:10,684 --> 00:04:11,664
bank account in panic.
